                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1ce7168b-a1d5-3b6f-9e4d-0cbde192bbab",
                                        "entry_id": "b066f9a5-04f9-3fa7-b1e0-460897847f11",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A scholar, teacher, priest, intellectual, researcher, scientist, knowledge-seeker, or knowledge worker."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e216597-14ae-37ba-bd57-0ad6e6e2b564",
                                        "entry_id": "b066f9a5-04f9-3fa7-b1e0-460897847f11",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A member of a social and cultural elite, especially in the New England region of the USA."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "New-England",
                                            "US",
                                            "capitalized",
                                            "especially"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "013bc53e-0478-420e-9996-8ee6c163ef25",
                                                "sense_id": "0e216597-14ae-37ba-bd57-0ad6e6e2b564",
                                                "text": "Branching from the root of it all was New England Society. The original Nelson [W. Aldrich] became remembered as a patrician, a Brahmin."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64cd6dc8-7575-4f9e-8b06-628ee073a662",
                                                "sense_id": "0e216597-14ae-37ba-bd57-0ad6e6e2b564",
                                                "text": "In Iran-Contra, the independent counsel investigating the scandal, Lawrence Walsh, was a deadly serious Brahmin lawyer with a sterling Republican pedigree; he nevertheless faced withering criticism from members of his own party, just as special counsel Robert Mueller has as he investigates Trump and his circle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a5c4f5e-c92f-33b6-87e2-4b76a07885cc",
                                        "entry_id": "b066f9a5-04f9-3fa7-b1e0-460897847f11",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A learned person of refined taste and mild manners."
                                        ],
